message.content:
{"diagnosis": "mem_la_addr[1:0] drives 2'b10 instead of 2'b00, matching TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero. Both fetch and data paths should be word-aligned with low bits 2'b00. Root cause is line 382 which builds mem_la_addr with {.., 2'b10} for both mux arms.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -382,1 +382,1 @@
-	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b10} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b10};
+	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};
", "expected": "tohost: PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero"}

